 "notes": "95% CL upper limit on the U(1)_B-L gauge coupling from Fig. 5 (figs/upperlimits_final.png in the e-print), pixel-extracted from the raster figure. The paper quotes epsilon_B-L, the gauge coupling normalized by the electromagnetic coupling e (Eq. 1: L contains -eps_D e J^mu_D A_mu); converted to the canonical gauge coupling via g_B-L = e * eps_B-L with e = sqrt(4*pi*alpha) = 0.3028. Fig. 5 shows two channels, MICH (blue) and PRCL (orange); reported is the pointwise minimum (best) of the two, with the very spiky trace reduced to per-log-bin medians (85 bins over the analyzed band 15-1015 Hz; noise-line spikes reach ~1e-15 in eps but the binned median tracks the limit floor). Mass from m_A = h*f. Axis calibration verified: recovered curve span 15.0-1013 Hz matches the stated 15-1015 Hz analysis range. Assumes standard halo model with rho_DM ~ 0.4 GeV/cm^3.",
